  "notes": "Suite-validated on 2026-11-10: the multisigned group's oid4vp-1final-wallet-multisigned-one-invalid-signature module PASSED against the engine (plan DVGvjpRfRL20v, suite 5.3.4) \u2014 the module invalidates the FIRST signature (the client's), leaving the second (the client2 fixture's) valid, and the wallet accepts: a failing signature is skipped, at least one valid one authenticates. The second signature's client_id (each protected header carries its cert's binding) is the one that authenticates; the invalidated signature's claim never does. The corrupted signature is the generated artifact's second with its tail replaced \u2014 verification against client2's cert fails. The request object is embedded verbatim at authoring time."
